# Line endings are part of this project's integrity hash, so they must not depend on
# the machine that checks the code out. Git on Windows defaults to converting LF to
# CRLF in the working copy, which would make the same commit hash differently after a
# fresh clone — a confusing "mismatch" that looks like tampering. Storing and
# checking out LF everywhere keeps the hash a property of the content.
* text=auto eol=lf
